Predefined globals a base installation declares (MYUSERNAME, CRLF,
UserLang) and the platform objects are never undeclared; CR and LF are
listed by the reference as NOT declared, so they flag with the Chr()
replacement in the message (diag.undeclared_variable, issue #270).
-- input.ssl --
:PROCEDURE BuildBanner;
	:DECLARE sBanner;
	sBanner := "User: " + MYUSERNAME + CRLF + "Lang: " + UserLang;
	sBanner := sBanner + CR + LF;
	sBanner += Session:SessionID;
	:RETURN sBanner;
:ENDPROC;
-- format --
:PROCEDURE BuildBanner;
	:DECLARE sBanner;

	sBanner := "User: " + MYUSERNAME + CRLF + "Lang: " + UserLang;
	sBanner := sBanner + CR + LF;
	sBanner += Session:SessionID;

	:RETURN sBanner;
:ENDPROC;
-- diagnostics --
-- diagnostics [--strict --info] --
4:23-4:25 warning undeclared_variable: Variable 'CR' is not declared; a base installation does not declare it as a global, use Chr(13) instead
4:28-4:30 warning undeclared_variable: Variable 'LF' is not declared; a base installation does not declare it as a global, use Chr(10) instead
